      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focusing on substance is the best strategy; let the weight of your ideas carry the academic tone. Instead of keyword stuffing, strategically weave in refined concepts that naturally embody those markers. For instance, articulate how your work challenges established understandings of technology's role in social structures to convey \"paradigm shift\" and \"epistemological\" concerns. This approach demonstrates intellectual maturity while still using high-level academic language appropriate for Oxford.",
      "source": "target",
